{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Problems and Solutions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Didn't Remember Having Met You Before", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Perfect -ing Forms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to talk about results and time, you can use a Perfect - ing form. You use this type of structure when you want to emphasize that one thing happens before another.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Having read your profile</span>, I think that we belong together.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this case, the action that comes first is <span class=\"italic\">Having read your profile</span> ... It is clear that the action <span class=\"italic\">I think that we belong together </span>comes last.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the Perfect - ing is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Having + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at the examples from the text. Think about which event happened first.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "After having received your business card, I went straight home and Googled you!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've got to say, having read your profile, I really do think that the universe just wants us to be together. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well, having cleared that up, let's talk about how we can arrange to bump into each other again, Boris. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reason Clauses: Because of, Due to, Owing to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to introduce a reason for a particular situation, you can use these prepositions at the beginning of the clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">because of </span>before a noun or a noun phrase.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We won't be able to make it <span class=\"strong\">because of the weather.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Due to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">owing to </span>also mean <span class=\"italic\">because of</span>. They sound a little more formal, and are therefore more common in professional English rather than conversational.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She was unable to attend the meeting <span class=\"strong\">due to a previous engagement.</span><br>We have less money to spend <span class=\"strong\">owing to the budget cuts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It's because of the name, really, that I knew we were destined to meet again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He's a little bit discombobulated due to the long flight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm befuddled because of a long one-hour flight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I must have grabbed the wrong one, owing to all of the confusion in the reception area.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bump into ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet someone unexpectedly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Martina! I certainly didn't expect to bump into you here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about a confusing situation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flattering ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "making someone look or feel good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She made a few flattering comments.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mess around ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be silly; not serious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Of course you're Adam. Stop messing around.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discombobulated ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused and unable to think clearly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He's a little bit discombobulated due to the long flight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get something straight ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to understand something clearly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I just want to get it straight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "befuddled ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm befuddled because of a long one-hour flight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flustered ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "upset and confused", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wow, you really are flustered today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to clear up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to explain a situation so that it is understood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, having cleared that up, let's talk about how we can arrange to bump into each other again, Boris.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to think straight ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think clearly or accurately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess I'm still not thinking straight, having just completed an epic 60-minute voyage. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write one sentence about something you did in your morning routine (e.g. I brushed my teeth).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Add another sentence, using the \u201cperfect\u201d with \u201c-ing\u201d form (e.g. After having brushed my teeth, I took a shower.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Continue adding sentences in the same manner, until you have completely described your morning routine.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe my morning routine.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I sequence events using the present perfect.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my ideas with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about results in time in work and job situation